  "message": "Here's who I can route work to and what each one does.\n\nmapper_cash — looks for vendor patterns in cash purchases.\nmapper_card — finds vendor patterns in card purchases.\nmapper_bank — finds vendor patterns in ACH payments and online transfers; good for recurring bills.\nmapper_other — analyzes checks and other uncategorized payment methods.\nsynthesizer — combines the four mapper reports and flags missed bills, unusual amounts, and possible new recurring expenses.\nreceipt_scanner — finds orphaned or mislabeled receipt images and checks them against the expenses database.\nexpense_reconciler — finds expenses without matching receipts (excluding transactions that don't need one).\nprogress_check — tells you which finance reports already exist and how fresh they are (reads reports only).\ncategory_spreadsheet — builds a read‑only spreadsheet of every expense in one named category from the real books.\nspreadsheet_reshaper — reshapes an existing combined expense spreadsheet into columns by person.\nagent_creator — builds a brand‑new helper agent from your description and registers it.\ntoyota_mechanic — diagnoses or improves my own code; runs tests in a sandbox and applies changes only if they pass.\nmechanic_translator — turns a vague request about my behavior or code into a precise instruction the mechanic can run.\ndashboard_expert — answers questions about and edits the Leta‑Code Dashboard codebase (read/write to that repo only).\nbrowser_opener — opens a literal URL or search phrase in the Windows browser on this box.\nsearch_link_opener — searches the web for a named site and opens the actual site result in the browser for you to log in.\n\nAlso Mazda is the bookkeeping agent I open on request; she handles statement intake, receipts, and the books on her dashboard page.\n\nIf you want me to run any of these now, tell me which one and what to check or build.",
